url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarosorio-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarosorio-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarosorio-dev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oscarosorio-dev","id":132024122,"login":"oscarosorio-dev","node_id":"U_kgDOB96HOg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarosorio-dev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarosorio-dev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarosorio-dev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarosorio-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarosorio-dev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oscarosorio-dev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarDamian/Onboarding-Candidate-Profile-Intelligence-Platform/commits/14f99fb8da0b21fdd251a899eecffced02b1b936/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-13T14:39:58Z","email":"132024122+OsOsorioP@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Oscar Osorio"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-13T14:39:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(week-3): microfrontend, robustness, llm fallback, automation of qdrant reindex and improvements\n\n### Summary\n\nDelivers foundational improvements aligned with the Week 3 goal of strengthening system robustness and modernizing the architecture. It introduces Redis-backed async job processing, improves API reliability and schema validation, hardens ETL pipelines, and adds LLM fallback support to increase resilience in production.\n\n#### Scope & Objectives\n\n- Improve platform robustness and fault tolerance.\n- Introduce async/background processing for heavy workloads (ETL, indexing, embeddings).\n- Standardize API error handling and validation.\n- Improve reliability of LLM integrations via fallback.\n- Update documentation and deployment configuration to reflect the new architecture.\n\n#### Key Changes\n1. API (FastAPI)\n\n- Standardized error handling via custom exceptions.\n- Improved OpenAPI documentation and response schemas.\n- Schema fixes and new search response contract.\n- Test configuration added.\n- LangChain integration with Groq fallback for LLM resilience.\n\n2. ETL & Pipelines\n\n- Field-level validation isolated and enforced.\n- Async full reindex pipeline enabled.\n- Improved reliability for batch processing (ETL / embeddings).\n\n3. Async Jobs & Redis\n\n- Redis-backed job queue for:\n- Candidate indexing\n- Candidate deletion\n- Full reindex\n- Redis caching layer for candidate insights.\n- Test updates for async workflows (Redis + Qdrant).\n- New environment variables: REDIS_URL, REDIS_QUEUE.\n\n4. Config & Docs\n\n- Environment and dependency updates.\n- README and architecture docs updated:\n- Error handling strategy\n- Async job processing\n- LLM fallback ADR\n\n#### Deployment Notes\n\nRedis must be available in the target environment.\n\nConfigure:\n\n- REDIS_URL\n\n- REDIS_QUEUE\n\n- Update dependencies before deploy.","tree":{"sha":"798cb0683e79613e8a752eb7dda7eb7d157dd458","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarDamian/Onboarding-Candidate-Profile-Intelligence-Platform/git/trees/798cb0683e79613e8a752eb7dda7eb7d157dd458"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MarDamian/Onboarding-Candidate-Profile-Intelligence-Platform/git/commits/14f99fb8da0b21fdd251a899eecffced02b1b936","verification":{"payload":"tree 798cb0683e79613e8a752eb7dda7eb7d157dd458\nparent e3a6c86a2a2c6e479ddd15e3b79b6fc97c4d9fd1\nparent e1e7153c8583eaeb55a038f0cdc9fb5998a05d5b\nauthor Oscar Osorio <132024122+OsOsorioP@users.noreply.github.com> 1770993598 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770993598 -0500\n\nfeat(week-3): microfrontend, robustness, llm fallback, automation of qdrant reindex and improvements\n\n### Summary\n\nDelivers foundational improvements aligned with the Week 3 goal of strengthening system robustness and modernizing the architecture. It introduces Redis-backed async job processing, improves API reliability and schema validation, hardens ETL pipelines, and adds LLM fallback support to increase resilience in production.\n\n#### Scope & Objectives\n\n- Improve platform robustness and fault tolerance.\n- Introduce async/background processing for heavy workloads (ETL, indexing, embeddings).\n- Standardize API error handling and validation.\n- Improve reliability of LLM integrations via fallback.\n- Update documentation and deployment configuration to reflect the new architecture.\n\n#### Key Changes\n1. API (FastAPI)\n\n- Standardized error handling via custom exceptions.\n- Improved OpenAPI documentation and response schemas.\n- Schema fixes and new search response contract.\n- Test configuration added.\n- LangChain integration with Groq fallback for LLM resilience.\n\n2. ETL & Pipelines\n\n- Field-level validation isolated and enforced.\n- Async full reindex pipeline enabled.\n- Improved reliability for batch processing (ETL / embeddings).\n\n3. Async Jobs & Redis\n\n- Redis-backed job queue for:\n- Candidate indexing\n- Candidate deletion\n- Full reindex\n- Redis caching layer for candidate insights.\n- Test updates for async workflows (Redis + Qdrant).\n- New environment variables: REDIS_URL, REDIS_QUEUE.\n\n4. Config & Docs\n\n- Environment and dependency updates.\n- README and architecture docs updated:\n- Error handling strategy\n- Async job processing\n- LLM fallback ADR\n\n#### Deployment Notes\n\nRedis must be available in the target environment.\n\nConfigure:\n\n- REDIS_URL\n\n- REDIS_QUEUE\n\n- Update dependencies before deploy.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpjze+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvUYQAKDiaBnC+EZSLqOX15w033pm\ntx/pZH7Xrh0mgx29GVU3X815hzXuVR+v4HlPMz4ImjZPrSpFlpTyxcSkQRP0hp6k\nr0FJDvM/NgtEDTm0ZwowZoeHP4dmRrRPiaH2HEX4l9ryQqZuOE2TzLjH4GdC1f5C\neki5wNAqh7yWOZk+B8lvDsZ/Aqe