m/esarafianou","id":17114347,"login":"esarafianou","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MTE0MzQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esarafianou","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/b9c2bd733fca307507cee1a7c788a250ea81b9e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T12:21:21Z","email":"eva.sarafianou@gmail.com","name":"Eva Sarafianou"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T12:21:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: restore generated plugin SDK reference pages (#37788)\n\n* docs: restore generated plugin SDK reference pages\n\nReimplements the Hugo-era plugingodocs/pluginjsdocs/pluginmanifestdocs\nshortcode pipeline natively in Docusaurus, so the server plugin SDK,\nweb app plugin SDK, and manifest reference pages render full generated\ncontent again instead of \"Generated content (migrating)\" placeholders.\n\nTwo new Go generators (gen-plugin-godocs, gen-plugin-manifest-docs) and\none Node generator (gen-plugin-jsdocs.mjs) read server/public/plugin,\nserver/public/model, and webapp/channels/src/plugins/registry.ts\ndirectly from this monorepo and emit gitignored JSON consumed by new\nPluginGoDocs/PluginGoExample/PluginJsDocs/PluginManifestDocs React\ncomponents, wired into prestart/prebuild alongside the existing\nsidebar/OpenAPI generators.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: remove migration plan doc from this PR\n\nWas a handoff/status doc for the implementing agent, not meant to ship\nas part of the change itself.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: make plugin-godocs/manifest-docs builds atomic\n\nbuild:plugin-godocs and build:plugin-manifest-docs redirected straight\ninto data/plugin-*.json, which doesn''t exist on a clean checkout (the\nredirection itself would fail before the generator ever ran) and, on a\nsubsequent failed run, would truncate a previously-good JSON file\nbefore failing. Create data/ up front, write to a .tmp file, and only\nmv it into place once the generator exits successfully.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: fix review findings in plugin doc generators\n\ngen-plugin-manifest-docs:\n- jsonFieldName now excludes unexported fields (matching encoding/json)\n  and falls back to the Go field name when there''s no tag or the tag''s\n  name component is empty (e.g. json:\",omitempty\"), instead of\n  dropping the field entirely.\n- exprTypeDocs''s SelectorExpr case now resolves a qualified type only\n  when its package qualifier actually points at the model package\n  (checked against the declaring file''s imports), instead of matching\n  any x.Sel identifier by name alone regardless of which package it\n  qualifies.\n\ngen-plugin-godocs:\n- The example-code loop now falls back to example.Code when\n  example.Play is nil (go/doc leaves Play nil when it can''t synthesize\n  a whole runnable program), and propagates printer.Fprint errors\n  instead of discarding them.\n\nNo output change for the current server/public/plugin or\nserver/public/model content — verified via a full regen.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: drop legacy-repo comment references, align jsdocs generator parser\n\nRemove \"port of the old mattermost-developer-documentation Hugo\nshortcode\" comments from the plugin doc generators/components now that\nthey''re fully native to this monorepo, and switch gen-plugin-jsdocs.mjs\nfrom the TypeScript compiler API to @typescript-eslint/typescript-estree\nto match the old script''s parser/shape, while keeping the more robust\nreArg-declared-parameter-name and node-scoped comment-attachment logic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: bump plugin doc generators'' go.mod to go 1.26\n\ngo 1.23 was arbitrarily low; align with a current Go version. go run\nauto-downloads a matching toolchain on older local installs, so this\ndoesn''t reintroduce a dependency on server/public/go.mod''s version.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: handle RestElement in gen-plugin-jsdocs parameter extraction\n\nparamNamesFromPattern silently dropped rest parameters/destructured rest\nmembers (e.g. (a, ...rest) or {a, ...rest}), since RestElement matched\nnone of its type checks. No effect on today''s registry.ts output (no\nrest patterns currently used there), but keeps the extraction correct if\none is ever introduced.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: simplify plugin doc generators README note\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: check stdout write errors in plugin doc generators\n\nos.Stdout.Write''s return errors were discarded, so a failed/partial\nwrite (e.g. broken pipe, disk full) would still exit 0. Combined with\nthe npm scripts'' > file.tmp && mv pattern, a truncated write could be\ntreated as a successful generation. Fatal on either write failing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: flatten Server/Webapp plugin SDK reference sidebar nesting\n\nserver/server-reference.md and webapp/webapp-reference.md were the only\nfile in their respective folders, so the sidebar generator (which only\ncollapses a folder into a single entry when it has an index.md) rendered\nthem as a \"Server\" > \"Server plugin SDK reference\" category with one\nchild instead of one flat entry, unlike every sibling reference folder\n(rest-api/index.md, bot-accounts/index.md, etc.).\n\nRename both to index.md to match that convention, and update the ~20\ncross-referencing links (many with #anchor fragments) that pointed at\nthe old /reference/server/server-reference and /reference/webapp/webapp-\nreference paths.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"412e9c93710bc41efa15049297fa0ba9e8fd5270","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/412e9c93710bc41efa15049297fa0ba9e8fd5270"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/b9c2bd733fca307507cee1a7c788a250ea81b9e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 412e9c93710bc41efa15049297fa0ba9e8fd5270\nparent 4881d14dc8e977bc4286be26420e61412008b477\nauthor Eva Sarafianou <eva.sarafianou@gmail.com> 1787314881 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787314881 +0300\n\ndocs: restore generated plugin SDK reference pages (#37788)\n\n* docs: restore generated plugin SDK reference pages\n\nReimplements the Hugo-era plugingodocs/pluginjsdocs/pluginmanifestdocs\nshortcode pipeline natively in Docusaurus, so the server plugin SDK,\nweb app plugin SDK, and manifest reference pages render full generated\ncontent again instead of \"Generated content (migrating)\" placeholders.\n\nTwo new Go generators (gen-plugin-godocs, gen-plugin-manifest-docs) and\none Node generator (gen-plugin-jsdocs.mjs) read server/public/plugin,\nserver/public/model, and webapp/channels/src/plugins/registry.ts\ndirectly from this monorepo and emit gitignored JSON consumed by new\nPluginGoDocs/PluginGoExample/PluginJsDocs/PluginManifestDocs React\ncomponents, wired into prestart/prebuild alongside the existing\nsidebar/OpenAPI generators.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: remove migration plan doc from this PR\n\nWas a handoff/status doc for the implementing agent, not meant to ship\nas part of the change itself.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: make plugin-godocs/manifest-docs builds atomic\n\nbuild:plugin-godocs and build:plugin-manifest-docs redirected straight\ninto data/plugin-*.json, which doesn''t exist on a clean checkout (the\nredirection itself would fail before the generator ever ran) and, on a\nsubsequent failed run, would truncate a previously-good JSON file\nbefore failing. Create data/ up front, write to a .tmp file, and only\nmv it into place once the generator exits successfully.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: fix review findings in plugin doc generators\n\ngen-plugin-manifest-docs:\n- jsonFieldName now excludes unexported fields (matching encoding/json)\n  and falls back to the Go field name when there''s no tag or the tag''s\n  name component is empty (e.g. json:\",omitempty\"), instead of\n  dropping the field entirely.\n- exprTypeDocs''s SelectorExpr case now resolves a qualified type only\n  when its package qualifier actually points at the model package\n  (checked against the declaring file''s imports), instead of matching\n  any x.Sel identifier by name alone regardless of which package it\n  qualifies.\n\ngen-plugin-godocs:\n- The example-code loop now falls back to example.Code when\n  example.Play is nil (go/doc leaves Play nil when it can''t synthesize\n  a whole runnable program), and propagates printer.Fprint errors\n  instead of discarding them.\n\nNo output change for the current server/public/plugin or\nserver/public/model content — verified via a full regen.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: drop legacy-repo comment references, align jsdocs generator parser\n\nRemove \"port of the old mattermost-developer-documentation Hugo\nshortcode\" comments from the plugin doc generators/components now that\nthey''re fully native to this monorepo, and switch gen-plugin-jsdocs.mjs\nfrom the TypeScript compiler API to @typescript-eslint/typescript-estree\nto match the old script''s parser/shape, while keeping the more robust\nreArg-declared-parameter-name and node-scoped comment-attachment logic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: bump plugin doc generators'' go.mod to go 1.26\n\ngo 1.23 was arbitrarily low; align with a current Go version. go run\nauto-downloads a matching toolchain on older local installs, so this\ndoesn''t reintroduce a dependency on server/public/go.mod''s version.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: handle RestElement in gen-plugin-jsdocs parameter extraction\n\nparamNamesFromPattern silently dropped rest parameters/destructured rest\nmembers (e.g. (a, ...rest) or {a, ...rest}), since RestElement matched\nnone of its type checks. No effect on today''s registry.ts output (no\nrest patterns currently used there), but keeps the extraction correct if\none is ever introduced.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: simplify plugin doc generators README note\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: check stdout write errors in plugin doc generators\n\nos.Stdout.Write''s return errors were discarded, so a failed/partial\nwrite (e.g. broken pipe, disk full) would still exit 0. Combined with\nthe npm scripts'' > file.tmp && mv pattern, a truncated write could be\ntreated as a successful generation. Fatal on either write failing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: flatten Server/Webapp plugin SDK reference sidebar nesting\n\nserver/server-reference.md and webapp/webapp-reference.md were the only\nfile in their respective folders, so the sidebar generator (which only\ncollapses a folder into a single entry when it has an index.md) rendered\nthem as a \"Server\" > \"Server plugin SDK reference\" category with one\nchild instead of one flat entry, unlike every sibling reference folder\n(rest-api/index.md, bot-accounts/index.md, etc.).\n\nRename both to index.md to match that convention, and update the ~20\ncross-referencing links (many with #anchor fragments) that pointed at\nthe old /reference/server/server-reference and /reference/webapp/webapp-\nreference paths.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiELBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM/UQAFtaAuyOgQz3GTE42RyfbEEp\n21fGSsABpJt6Ko6cA9r3HtOoaKsWkxuOVToG8o/cuTvAYaUlKyWqIEXn46Fr5TQL\n/jqbaN1LBESaPA80bUjdIWs43Xkf/W9yMNQKjMcfHmX+rZnHP3Ifeudb3PXK6y7f\n8bqFVmc64e5dNKKq5xg9Jq4Zt7N8FzokVbI2nCa02bQXGW4urQGawTLWanjIRjLq\nX9IHrM4e3TPo38Um4QR9pozsbElDMySPiTnfWeR5AGQtKZF83PgkGnMky0TrB0+r\nIOZ8MY/QG7bbzbCB8PxMhBVMJksNO0sJsbihQnBEZgau7C8MZ8BLFXmrXu3D3W1r\n3q1iT2OImkOeJTaGX9SkVz+F59q5oY1QgP+R6M2dW0C+T5Yyfodu9bcD0tPrbCJG\nNKp/29in0BDxwCm8GrCJ9BKNPuUM9jZVCsZjhgnhLmw/a6hl75Db5twR3FIO7MdS\nCnzuIxRRoLg3VOaugfpqW88F/jgnqqNVdoKMOsX8xJyo0Breo9dGqWLsfk2kN9MY\nenXzsHl5BhuEnDrhnZOJirapMhROR7pitpg5G7knLj/uroWQh9ZLH8JEQtvoIMpS\nFCU7zQLhLXWl0Xnw0E6LsEvGsfqy1H9u2EYFGDLILa7OAXkM440HswvAQMN9nmCT\n47KnwZMk4ncSjF5+qBGM\n=ZLnf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T12:21:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/b9c2bd733fca307507cee1a7c788a250ea81b9e3","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKGI5YzJiZDczM2ZjYTMwNzUwN2NlZTFhN2M3ODhhMjUwZWE4MWI5ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/4881d14dc8e977bc4286be26420e61412008b477","sha":"4881d14dc8e977bc4286be26420e61412008b477","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/4881d14dc8e977bc4286be26420e61412008b477"}],"sha":"b9c2bd733fca307507cee1a7c788a250ea81b9e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/b9c2bd733fca307507cee1a7c788a250ea81b9e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12176405?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nickmisasi","id":12176405,"login":"nickmisasi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTc2NDA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/4881d14dc8e977bc4286be26420e61412008b477/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T12:09:10Z","email":"nick.misasi@mattermost.com","name":"Nick Misasi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T12:09:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix Avatar layout regressions from MM-69802 without collapsing size tokens (#38072)\n\n* Fix Avatar layout regressions from MM-69802 without font-size:0\n\nBroken images are no longer replaced elements, so width/height stop\napplying and alt text sizes the box. Use inline-block plus overflow and\ntransparent color so the existing size tokens still apply and alt text\ncannot spill out of the circle.\n\nThis restores em margins (scheduled/drafts DM avatars) and flex min-width\n(agent selector, post previews), and removes the Content Flagging\npreview spot-patch from #37972.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nick13misasi@gmail.com>\n\n* Trigger Enterprise CI after mostest_password fix\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nick13misasi@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"7f1bc293c7cf1949533f633a73e4b4b1322bfbea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/7f1bc293c7cf1949533f633a73e4b4b1322bfbea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/4881d14dc8e977bc4286be26420e61412008b477","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f1bc293c7cf1949533f633a73e4b4b1322bfbea\nparent 6ac8899d93c070330bae7b73cfd5468205720089\nauthor Nick Misasi <nick.misasi@mattermost.com> 1787314150 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787314150 +0000\n\nFix Avatar layout regressions from MM-69802 without collapsing size tokens (#38072)\n\n* Fix Avatar layout regressions from MM-69802 without font-size:0\n\nBroken images are no longer replaced elements, so width/height stop\napplying and alt text sizes the box. Use inline-block plus overflow and\ntransparent color so the existing size tokens still apply and alt text\ncannot spill out of the circle.\n\nThis restores em margins (scheduled/drafts DM avatars) and flex min-width\n(agent selector, post previews), and removes the Content Flagging\npreview spot-patch from #37972.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nick13misasi@gmail.com>\n\n* Trigger Enterprise CI after mostest_password fix\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nick13misasi@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiD/mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWpQQADBrvX7DisPBu1mx5IpBDGYd\nGMCmoa/ndRRqe03asPZSN799nBFYij0nlR/4msoDyvxk3SLQDzHOkRC09aiUYo7H\nDS93HSQEZlmmzBmp4+leSAhWr6rtrBpDKrq078hQcN3WyZDORBMH37zxnQcECLCX\nOfTSxzO8Er8ngNpoFxi9WKfRcrH+yFcRp6yRepN0+75jw2zuDvVxIzdWoWWXG6+q\nB7BgtsyAzgkw8HpDRQmI99H689kPJRJZ5Lf7GBwdurKiwQIX1+C5kcl8QP3Uii4Q\nyuHUCMPVFyNtcRWPe/Q2vvqHqOpQzJ8E9ub3xTzWI1mTSNgHqb9Y5C3zNc3Ud+4S\nJ24MaFLWvV1mDgvF23kNeSVgSWKQm/k+9TLX7Hbn0pbcHA+GYawxug5megUqB8ex\noDbk5+dOnjrLLpqNEaSP68fj0PBqZZY1RyFKgFJ2uAYhW33Tu08NpYW2UUwGOFUF\ni+etLwre4+GCEHi7tDJ4KxZjX9YD4MJpAHpDlqo8kEIPHVlC50cq8hzh/JJBIgU3\nL886AKHicdtUE/BqDOD4DKygWNM4RAIzKh9h4z70lSVEoHvTkYWugbxci6xnomSk\nu1hx8RNp9jJDpFDjXjlhBJxDDG9/JaKbwcAqMjCV0fCMEUye02j5Yf5aVONmdvK5\nhg7KvczWTY//Mpe6Wr8g\n=mATr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T12:09:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/4881d14dc8e977bc4286be26420e61412008b477","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKDQ4ODFkMTRkYzhlOTc3YmM0Mjg2YmUyNjQyMGU2MTQxMjAwOGI0Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/6ac8899d93c070330bae7b73cfd5468205720089","sha":"6ac8899d93c070330bae7b73cfd5468205720089","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/6ac8899d93c070330bae7b73cfd5468205720089"}],"sha":"4881d14dc8e977bc4286be26420e61412008b477","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/4881d14dc8e977bc4286be26420e61412008b477"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3924815?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/agarciamontoro","id":3924815,"login":"agarciamontoro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MjQ4MTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/agarciamontoro","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/6ac8899d93c070330bae7b73cfd5468205720089/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T10:52:52Z","email":"alejandro.garciamontoro@gmail.com","name":"Alejandro García Montoro"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T10:52:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MM-70307: Bump Go version to v1.26.7 (#38046)\n\n* Bump Go version to v1.26.7\n\n* Fix digest\n\n* Update glibc to v16 in runtime image as well\n\n* Trigger E2E tests\n\n* MM-70307: Fix FIPS E2E test failure due to short PostgreSQL password\n\nOpenSSL FIPS requires HMAC keys to be at least 14 bytes (112 bits). The\npassword ''mostest'' (6 bytes) triggers a panic in lib/pq''s SCRAM-SHA-256\nauthentication when the server runs under go-msft-fips with the\nglibc-openssl-fips:16 image. Replace it with ''mostest_password'' (16\nbytes) in all E2E test PostgreSQL connection strings and container\nconfigs. LDAP admin passwords are unaffected (different protocol).\n\n* Revert \"MM-70307: Fix FIPS E2E test failure due to short PostgreSQL password\"\n\nThis reverts commit d31b0eb5e8a025a8e30b7108483f5ba6da7bf9dd.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"dbdf60f9d8deb1dcfc31830c2e9783888731885b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/dbdf60f9d8deb1dcfc31830c2e9783888731885b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/6ac8899d93c070330bae7b73cfd5468205720089","verification":{"payload":"tree dbdf60f9d8deb1dcfc31830c2e9783888731885b\nparent cce8fdff7610963c5eb284525f5fc3414fd7c9b1\nauthor Alejandro García Montoro <alejandro.garciamontoro@gmail.com> 1787309572 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787309572 +0200\n\nMM-70307: Bump Go version to v1.26.7 (#38046)\n\n* Bump Go version to v1.26.7\n\n* Fix digest\n\n* Update glibc to v16 in runtime image as well\n\n* Trigger E2E tests\n\n* MM-70307: Fix FIPS E2E test failure due to short PostgreSQL password\n\nOpenSSL FIPS requires HMAC keys to be at least 14 bytes (112 bits). The\npassword ''mostest'' (6 bytes) triggers a panic in lib/pq''s SCRAM-SHA-256\nauthentication when the server runs under go-msft-fips with the\nglibc-openssl-fips:16 image. Replace it with ''mostest_password'' (16\nbytes) in all E2E test PostgreSQL connection strings and container\nconfigs. LDAP admin passwords are unaffected (different protocol).\n\n* Revert \"MM-70307: Fix FIPS E2E test failure due to short PostgreSQL password\"\n\nThis reverts commit d31b0eb5e8a025a8e30b7108483f5ba6da7bf9dd.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiC4ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZVQQAJb6UJrPZsEzJ7I8sCrwu73k\n5zs7UFCN1zDc3jJ5/YwLq14nWvlTwirkY6Wc+m9brFvq8fhpWM1PFKq7bAWgT33Z\nthDq2yJyk7mOx+w7Fokx+aIugz8hSKbSjGlQl6QfZGLdW6ixAMHcQny9Swl8clyC\n0oAcV2rbhiruuxy0BROziiJlkI7fDGw7nv0oTbNq5BgfXhg7ZbJvv5bm/x+eIk7E\nSpH3886xNgm883gKrQPqG1b6lBcgPZACxuIxZaGg66USOGANf4LEjdjaHtxqGQVv\nxTut6rsuQwRDGLUl9LlKyW6SlpVuUdvySCG4rtVMu7NmshW7t+6kMyeWa8P1zP9b\nqxUHKve0PNpDCfTfr4nmWQMBPdKCsPq4sVHzD7qcGS2oQvroA/FhpR6McA1DvVLa\nvXeH2XGekmn3eqvrcweuNCsHezodPPkSWMxjG/Ra+VOpGmVfYFwJfih21JgzsdLQ\nXidJ0I5vi13q5qATCeeS8zcjHzsfplURseUdQ/HrueyWK4bKE2l7ar74n/tFm5a2\nwIUFCOQr+MwwpgPMuoab2xKFV3h98d/3dPwM886zwUmQjNA/LMdP6oJHwTMNZ0Fp\nAa8T3tmU8nnlFJ68eqMHJU9g9sxRGaDI8Xhu4XFFJ+Xk9mHTxKQoNQ8w9odsJ05h\nfpUlRoLBbDLIb24Cm9gU\n=v8fR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T10:52:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_event