ithub.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/ca6fd94e3d10a18b8feb03d3f612adae6e5de4f7","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKGNhNmZkOTRlM2QxMGExOGI4ZmViMDNkM2Y2MTJhZGFlNmU1ZGU0Zjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/6941f569018775c17062ab1118c6df84386a28ad","sha":"6941f569018775c17062ab1118c6df84386a28ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/6941f569018775c17062ab1118c6df84386a28ad"}],"sha":"ca6fd94e3d10a18b8feb03d3f612adae6e5de4f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/ca6fd94e3d10a18b8feb03d3f612adae6e5de4f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/6941f569018775c17062ab1118c6df84386a28ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:05:10Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T07:05:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-70252] Return 400 for malformed date filters in logs query API (#37970)\n\n* [MM-70252] Reject malformed date filters in logs query API\n\nThe POST /api/v4/logs/query endpoint parsed date_from/date_to with a fixed\nlayout and swallowed parse errors, silently dropping the bound instead of\nsignalling the caller. A malformed date_from became the zero time and a\nmalformed date_to became now, so the request returned HTTP 200 with an\nunfiltered result set.\n\nAdd LogFilter.IsValid, which rejects a non-empty bound that cannot be parsed\nwith the shared LogFilterDateLayout while keeping empty strings meaning\n\"unbounded\", and call it from queryLogs so a bad filter returns 400 naming the\noffending field and the expected layout.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Add tests for logs query date filter validation\n\nAdd a unit test for LogFilter.IsValid covering empty (unbounded), valid, and\nmalformed bounds, and an api4 integration test that drives POST /logs/query\nthrough the real router to assert malformed date_from/date_to return 400 with\nthe offending field id while empty and valid bounds return 200.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Harden logs query date filter tests\n\nAddress test-quality review: exercise the DateTo validation branch with a valid\nnon-empty DateFrom, move fallible checks out of the require.Eventually condition\nto avoid a cross-goroutine failure, and make each api4 subtest self-contained by\npolling for the expected messages via a shared helper so valid-bounds also\nverifies filtering still returns records.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Retrigger CI/CodeRabbit after invalid public-module feedback\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Note shared LogFilterDateLayout usage in date filter\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Add Client4.QueryLogs to simplify logs query date filter tests\n\n* Address PR feedback: 2 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <ben.schumacher@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"6040e1d199c2201704c862274bbde838d581bbd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/6040e1d199c2201704c862274bbde838d581bbd9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/6941f569018775c17062ab1118c6df84386a28ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 6040e1d199c2201704c862274bbde838d581bbd9\nparent 480c1c5ed1688a9502d98f74c84675034f2f1ad9\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1787123110 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787123110 +0200\n\n[MM-70252] Return 400 for malformed date filters in logs query API (#37970)\n\n* [MM-70252] Reject malformed date filters in logs query API\n\nThe POST /api/v4/logs/query endpoint parsed date_from/date_to with a fixed\nlayout and swallowed parse errors, silently dropping the bound instead of\nsignalling the caller. A malformed date_from became the zero time and a\nmalformed date_to became now, so the request returned HTTP 200 with an\nunfiltered result set.\n\nAdd LogFilter.IsValid, which rejects a non-empty bound that cannot be parsed\nwith the shared LogFilterDateLayout while keeping empty strings meaning\n\"unbounded\", and call it from queryLogs so a bad filter returns 400 naming the\noffending field and the expected layout.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Add tests for logs query date filter validation\n\nAdd a unit test for LogFilter.IsValid covering empty (unbounded), valid, and\nmalformed bounds, and an api4 integration test that drives POST /logs/query\nthrough the real router to assert malformed date_from/date_to return 400 with\nthe offending field id while empty and valid bounds return 200.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Harden logs query date filter tests\n\nAddress test-quality review: exercise the DateTo validation branch with a valid\nnon-empty DateFrom, move fallible checks out of the require.Eventually condition\nto avoid a cross-goroutine failure, and make each api4 subtest self-contained by\npolling for the expected messages via a shared helper so valid-bounds also\nverifies filtering still returns records.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Retrigger CI/CodeRabbit after invalid public-module feedback\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Note shared LogFilterDateLayout usage in date filter\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70252] Add Client4.QueryLogs to simplify logs query date filter tests\n\n* Address PR feedback: 2 answered, 1 resolved, 0 declined\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ben Schumacher <ben.schumacher@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhVWmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWiMQAJUUzfU3qSM/v7CBFrKfTZ5f\n0ZxSz8ZqEu/2iEVf+/DEyTTvBaIDJCKDX6js1GTeJWUlY8y3JVrfXGewgaQfTYx9\nFlrDixrBGOcIkmB8et1RVpkSNs4/bDYU4jACla2So9JjtBQDzG5jU8a8UvW0+xdz\n9PRrrMfKd1gZW63lvkOp6FDkGomp8gQTtxz2QvXpnC62TABsoo5XjuAorT6V4daG\nC8nY4ncrGo5UZq6cbvEzycsUdc7bqedduG6Aa1Rl4ddbcdc83e3DkK7+sXzXqTNm\naa9WH5IEkst5YytCvxcGxvOLyhVXMx/Ht41OnavcMitYhvp8/+l2abgmkjrlBbru\n+U2D4xjBbq+UePjydE5Im2jLTbIa/awQB9/ocl2YMD/W0tUghil7815BaRsugyaQ\nr633g4T5PWPcwzvg8qG+SD1Pg/gp6y+Obhz9pnZAAYGNE4MiLWWoSlmO1B/EBh9o\nbOvqQNv0pXfZ+rwx3XhjVk0aAu5WbO+x3Yx8NzqCpvE7KX6jKGDDJy1BExE1mt1U\n5CGBmBAEsXeMVwzINx/qFBmsxdkBm9Lx4G2Gtg+0s4JmqaHOjF1RG9WybwZNatDE\nxnVtyVqRn3S/BAU3qG+uUM7YUsRdYhe2x/HXA4wlN