llowers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/a234862de7da948f1869867a75349c03a20c2665","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKGEyMzQ4NjJkZTdkYTk0OGYxODY5ODY3YTc1MzQ5YzAzYTIwYzI2NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/4f8b9d8195ef527f279c2a02f3d24ea87284af1f","sha":"4f8b9d8195ef527f279c2a02f3d24ea87284af1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/4f8b9d8195ef527f279c2a02f3d24ea87284af1f"}],"sha":"a234862de7da948f1869867a75349c03a20c2665","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/a234862de7da948f1869867a75349c03a20c2665"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1023171?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lieut-data","id":1023171,"login":"lieut-data","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjMxNzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lieut-data","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/4f8b9d8195ef527f279c2a02f3d24ea87284af1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T11:32:19Z","email":"jesse.hallam@gmail.com","name":"Jesse Hallam"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T11:32:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-69641] Promote EnableExportDirectDownload to a Cloud-only configuration setting (#37477)\n\n* promote EnableExportDirectDownload to a Cloud-only configuration setting\n\nReplace the FeatureFlags.EnableExportDirectDownload feature flag with a\nFileSettings.EnableCloudExportDirectDownload configuration setting, gated\nto Mattermost Cloud environments.\n\nThe /exportlink slash command and the export generate-presigned-url API\nnow require FileSettings.EnableCloudExportDirectDownload to be enabled and\na Cloud license. Operators previously enabling the feature via\nMM_FEATUREFLAGS_ENABLEEXPORTDIRECTDOWNLOAD should transition to\nMM_FILESETTINGS_ENABLECLOUDEXPORTDIRECTDOWNLOAD.\n\n* add tests for Cloud-only export direct download gating\n\nCover the new EnableCloudExportDirectDownload + Cloud-license gate on\nGeneratePresignURLForExport (app) and the generate-presigned-url API\n(api4).\n\n* add EnableCloudExportDirectDownload to FileSettings type\n\n* gate export direct download on Cloud alone, without a configuration setting\n\n* Use a bounded HTTP client in export presigned-URL tests\n\nhttp.Get has no total timeout; if MinIO accepts the connection but\nstalls, these tests can hang until the suite timeout.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab3dc81b202813185aa5ab377e5e5e140af76016","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/ab3dc81b202813185aa5ab377e5e5e140af76016"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/4f8b9d8195ef527f279c2a02f3d24ea87284af1f","verification":{"payload":"tree ab3dc81b202813185aa5ab377e5e5e140af76016\nparent d18f3dd278889d2644007f96fda3ccc7ebe0d4c6\nauthor Jesse Hallam <jesse.hallam@gmail.com> 1786707139 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786707139 +0000\n\n[MM-69641] Promote EnableExportDirectDownload to a Cloud-only configuration setting (#37477)\n\n* promote EnableExportDirectDownload to a Cloud-only configuration setting\n\nReplace the FeatureFlags.EnableExportDirectDownload feature flag with a\nFileSettings.EnableCloudExportDirectDownload configuration setting, gated\nto Mattermost Cloud environments.\n\nThe /exportlink slash command and the export generate-presigned-url API\nnow require FileSettings.EnableCloudExportDirectDownload to be enabled and\na Cloud license. Operators previously enabling the feature via\nMM_FEATUREFLAGS_ENABLEEXPORTDIRECTDOWNLOAD should transition to\nMM_FILESETTINGS_ENABLECLOUDEXPORTDIRECTDOWNLOAD.\n\n* add tests for Cloud-only export direct download gating\n\nCover the new EnableCloudExportDirectDownload + Cloud-license gate on\nGeneratePresignURLForExport (app) and the generate-presigned-url API\n(api4).\n\n* add EnableCloudExportDirectDownload to FileSettings type\n\n* gate export direct download on Cloud alone, without a configuration setting\n\n* Use a bounded HTTP client in export presigned-URL tests\n\nhttp.Get has no total timeout; if MinIO accepts the connection but\nstalls, these tests can hang until the suite timeout.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfvzDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2T4QADt15rBYh2uVvlitsZkzwaoH\ndeQ6Drtblc1j22vo+93mer7/XZ908wAWjiNxRJh+1RcuPXmMy17YB+UyMJzo5mqN\nDtL5oCy4D/W8Vua79xSVQM209LciubQF1pBOqXxHtVzS0CIVpQZE+9dWzKnz3xcw\n6J+x+rYzQEo6VwQ+6LYymOgZnB744QuXFHN3RAJL+WAIrsswScqKgmuBatV3Y2Or\nqIsUROL40pliKISkkthHEJp42gG+sX98FHlP415yacjgvXgpkPBoKpFZQ1aeduNm\nm4OhtJU0H73UbWbPsV2YtJlAb35O1IakBR3k7ST9YStyQXNvLnLkB+Ly2mTUj5zW\ncg55V0DvU9k5W1UkkWvdyVYLsJLQWLMOsHd7DM37XbcZCAc2XR+Et26AjF5E/ong\nXqnuaohUYtLYBl0tpRAUxmPOqomdotsDmPb+stc6lY6sIiGYHEtC5uhWSXBwlVK8\n9OdKGf1J/r1PaMNKfqKwm0KH6AbD3JYiKIpPnYSAjCrJeMTtnSU24p0wHiEHMsMe\n0QPNxC1BkOY7a5YPB6ZUt0+NMSq7yTeRqBeOyWG/i41Wmc0Ywsuoqf1/PCDGbElA\nz7ua8JuJ1E7XkxscJ7XWq8tUcXLEYBWFzJQIpbqJ4yhU6MbzkCbIMvTaGr2/mX6J\n4lQASV4VFL8hZ1fPZ+SJ\n=4UuP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T11:32:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/4f8b9d8195ef527f279c2a02f3d24ea87284af1f","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKDRmOGI5ZDgxOTVlZjUyN2YyNzljMmEwMmYzZDI0ZWE4NzI4NGFmMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/d18f3dd278889d2644007f96fda3ccc7ebe0d4c6","sha":"d18f3dd278889d2644007f96fda3ccc7ebe0d4c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/d18f3dd278889d2644007f96fda3ccc7ebe0d4c6"}],"sha":"4f8b9d8195ef527f279c2a02f3d24ea87284af1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/4f8b9d8195ef527f279c2a02f3d24ea87284af1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/d18f3dd278889d2644007f96fda3ccc7ebe0d4c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T08:39:53Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T08:39:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-69748] Add Hide Archived toggle to the Browse Channels modal (#37500)\n\n* [MM-69748] Add Hide Archived toggle to Browse Channels modal\n\nArchived channels previously appeared mixed in with active channels in\nthe Browse Channels modal under the default \"All channel types\" filter\n(most visibly in search results), with no way to filter them out.\n\nAdd a \"Hide Archived\" checkbox next to \"Hide Joined\" that hides archived\nchannels by default. The toggle is backed by a persisted preference and\nis not shown when the explicit \"Archived channels\" filter is selected.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69748] Add tests for Hide Archived toggle in Browse Channels\n\nCover the default-hidden behavior, toggling to show archived channels,\nthe explicit Archived filter override, preference persistence, and the\ncheckbox being hidden on the Archived filter.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69748] Strengthen Hide Archived tests per review\n\nAdd non-search browse-list coverage for getActiveChannels in both\ndirections, assert only archived rows are filtered from search, and\nquery the checkbox by accessible label.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Fix archived channel leak/duplication in Browse Channels filters\n\n- Exclude archived private channels from the private channels selector so\n  they no longer bypass the Hide Archived toggle or duplicate with the\n  archived list.\n- Fold archived channels back into the Public/Private lists (by type) when\n  the toggle is off, matching the All list behavior.\n- Keep the search Public filter governed by the shared hide-archived block\n  instead of hard-excluding archived public channels.\n- Add regression tests for the mixed public/private archived scenario.\n\n* Satisfy eslint style rules in browse channels changes\n\n* Update Browse Channels E2E for Hide Archived default\n\nAlign Cypress search expectations and Playwright tab/aria\nsnapshots with the new Hide Archived checkbox (on by default).\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"1224621dc39c01233e06bdf58828953b79570a45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/1224621dc39c01233e06bdf58828953b79570a45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/d18f3dd278889d2644007f96fda3ccc7ebe0d4c6","verification":{"payload":"tree 1224621dc39c01233e06bdf58828953b79570a45\nparent 22eaa8b03bbe2deb4728f4cf5cd5e870b90c6539\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1786696793 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786696793 +0200\n\n[MM-69748] Add Hide Archived toggle to the Browse Channels modal (#37500)\n\n* [MM-69748] Add Hide Archived toggle to Browse Channels modal\n\nArchived channels previously appeared mixed in with active channels in\nthe Browse Channels modal under the default \"All channel types\" filter\n(most visibly in search results), with no way to filter them out.\n\nAdd a \"Hide Archived\" checkbox next to \"Hide Joined\" that hides archived\nchannels by default. The toggle is backed by a persisted preference and\nis not shown when the explicit \"Archived channels\" filter is selected.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69748] Add tests for Hide Archived toggle in Browse Channels\n\nCover the default-hidden behavior, toggling to show archived channels,\nthe explicit Archived filter override, preference persistence, and the\ncheckbox being hidden on the Archived filter.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69748] Strengthen Hide Archived tests per review\n\nAdd non-search browse-list coverage for getActiveChannels in both\ndirections, assert only archived rows are filtered from search, and\nquery the checkbox by accessible label.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Fix archived channel leak/duplication in Browse Channels filters\n\n- Exclude archived private channels from the private channels selector so\n  they no longer bypass the Hide Archived toggle or duplicate with the\n  archived list.\n- Fold archived channels back into the Public/Private lists (by type) when\n  the toggle is off, matching the All list behavior.\n- Keep the search Public filter governed by the shared hide-archived block\n  instead of hard-excluding archived public channels.\n- Add regression tests for the mixed public/private archived scenario.\n\n* Satisfy eslint style rules in browse channels changes\n\n* Update Browse Channels E2E for Hide Archived default\n\nAlign Cypress search expectations and Playwright tab/aria\nsnapshots with the new Hide Archived checkbox (on by default).\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqftRZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZY0QAHka60DNCK9ZGuMlh1NrHDbn\nyiZYqxzQlPdUIu7V8B57JMEgzMgcUm3+6g9+Z8LmMChIQpkIlP6JA9tzFIQf0ukq\n/md2Ue1xD9CvXrPcEvJC0rGwCyLEPL0DvWma5LXf62QbrkdVDrivayJ0+E7QA3HQ\nz2jmcIZIPY7qpmYji6bpi1toEU6O46q14XAXxN4wy4BUwj4Gzc3J+aBY2kOCQ/MS\nVKB+zTtHqBJ2FUVHBm+O+PZIQFPSRSka0QX+N4HdKFAeFI86igWHKDzwoG82U7sF\nb64m5CfXzjBlx1jXZCFrljiS0EaVxZq9ytSW2zQ4u3yBMe2ri0QWMR/3u+S3y1NP\n43UsblKnyCn7ymVeFA8CfWTnexMbFnSm/V16TsdsIszDWhnz6Uq0+5wDlJpe8jyj\n5vDTtHz8oSrWwOHnc7JSAW5c1ilT299pQXCgGS2y/9TmJKh15JUmuZFV8Xuy1qGC\nijHnZHBYDHnCcj7f/mAHMueEYIkMcY3N9aXQfuFs9UD13SAICqYx/mDqQxfHYiR1\n2hx1XUU8e/d5id2GEzT4/tjKnpSsu362ueG1Syyb+v8WXSzg1RvxEkIwNZn++Nt5\n6Wv2iSRuXc8p/7nF9rI4Jp3Q1656VfdDpRXbEULIMgBqG1K/ItBEiv0agaXFXoNN\ndgngCDSFINuUS5w+PUXV\n=A4lb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T08:39:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/d18f3dd278889d2644007f96fda3ccc7ebe0d4c6","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKGQxOGYzZGQyNzg4ODlkMjY0NDAwN2Y5NmZkYTNjY2M3ZWJlMGQ0YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/22eaa8b03bbe2deb4728f4cf5cd5e870b90c6539","sha":"22eaa8b03bbe2deb4728f4cf5cd5e870b90c6539","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/22eaa8b03bbe2deb4728f4cf5cd5e870b90c6539"}],"sha":"d18f3dd278889d2644007f96fda3ccc7ebe0d4c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/d18f3dd278889d2644007f96fda3ccc7ebe0d4c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14200393?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bgardner8008","id":14200393,"login":"bgardner8008","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjAwMzkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bgardner8008","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/22eaa8b03bbe2deb4728f4cf5cd5e870b90c6539/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:36:17Z","email":"billg@wavearts.com","name":"Bill Gardner"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T07:36:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-69889] Improve handling of RelayState in SAML flow (#37837)\n\n* [MM-69889] Improve handling of RelayState in SAML flow\n\nRelayState was base64-decoded and trusted without any integrity check,\nletting its contents be tampered with client-side. Sign relayProps with\nan HMAC key (generated once, cached, stored like AsymmetricSigningKey)\nbefore handing it to the IdP, and verify the signature before trusting\nany of its fields on the way back.\n\n* Add short expiry to signed RelayState\n\nBound the signed RelayState''s validity to 5 minutes to restrict the\nwindow in which a captured, unmodified RelayState could be replayed.\n\n* [MM-69889] Use maps.Copy in SignSamlRelayState\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"3159b4629ef712725958d7f61cbdb0b249cbb5e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/3159b4629ef712725958d7f61cbdb0b249cbb5e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/22eaa8b03bbe2deb4728f4cf5cd5e870b90c6539","verification":{"payload":"tree 3159b4629ef712725958d7f61cbdb0b249cbb5e5\nparent 663ad3dae93f9eaf0c8ce01afa87bafdf7f22b71\nauthor Bill Gardner <billg@wavearts.com> 1786692977 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786692977 +0200\n\n[MM-69889] Improve handling of RelayState in SAML flow (#37837)\n\n* [MM-69889] Improve handling of RelayState in SAML flow\n\nRelayState was base64-decoded and trusted without any integrity check,\nletting its contents be tampered with client-side. Sign relayProps with\nan HMAC key (generated once, cached, stored like AsymmetricSigningKey)\nbefore handing it to the IdP, and verify the signature before trusting\nany of its fields on the way back.\n\n* Add short expiry to signed RelayState\n\nBound the signed RelayState''s validity to 5 minutes to restrict the\nwindow in which a captured, unmodified RelayState could be replayed.\n\n* [MM-69889] Use maps.Copy in SignSamlRelayState\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfsVxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeJsQACjw2ljNY4MK74doBlSZhvXS\neJfNFN/ilQK2iS812koBlsN6sR77LXtP4XPQpN48XH9v0v+VUmb9N17jCXaMfu4k\nbnShotNrmfTNp9QssFA0TMxpBs/pK3eDErUvMGkIg6/K0tPE9gYFPo9jGcsv949T\nWIHkBNPxljWxVhWdwNdhp/iKa+G8+01wl4M+DmxNlQa86zlZAocIV5jPcAQcbj8o\nJGYreqkKuo3VFN2kFPG4E5MwjYEmesWH1+QJ5z8dl0vANgUomCgWQBT5evJGlQ0T\nWOoxQDaLtuV8xKb2+Zfo/banTimpnCosaHDe7Ys2qLYyzlO2X1+QE/DYI4CDIItW\nki+da/dRUSsxkH7c6LnlV6BjrX2cEw2vl+qjSUxmZ8oC/xrVUtgvmX8llFYYPYP7\n3FUTqQe+xqBSAep0QukY1Hgowbb+ab8Yg+6bKctqitZ6VsslDZ3yR7baMrB2JR1g\nAtj97vvps6Tb35MtgGfBvTqw7SlF+jOV/qmuJqOYIxx6Ny9bBPn82XeCKZT9ZxWT\nnqHBmuCGT0tzPkVm/oLvpuB3yphvOywtekvw61EA9qCCnHYpL2sM4zudeQSa0Oht\nm+GFVBdX5TPhd+NfV/pajYl9JMHMzeX1/DGWzqg2Qj76cIJu/MBiBvf1bueQ+KOb\n86twRdjFOBgayBwFXAAd\n=XWfh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T07:36:21