"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/929a2e9e3f908c09b0582cea75433b2a482bc019"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4973621?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sudheerDev","id":4973621,"login":"sudheerDev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NzM2MjE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sudheerDev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/81d6d1ea20c07d9394cb569e7dd4da546cfc56fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:39:59Z","email":"sudheer.105@gmail.com","name":"Sudheer"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T14:39:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix link preview image layout shift by using SizeAwareImage (#37357)\n\n* Fix link preview image layout shift by reserving space with SizeAwareImage\n\nOpen graph link previews rendered a plain <img> with no upfront dimensions.\nWhen metadata reported large images (e.g. 2400×1256), the preview started at\nzero height and expanded after load, pushing content below and causing scroll\npop in the channel and permalink views.\n\nUse SizeAwareImage (same approach as post images and message attachments) so\nknown dimensions reserve layout before the image loads. Add\ngetScaledImageDimensions() to scale metadata down to the preview''s CSS limits\n(392×240 for large images, 80×80 for thumbnails) so placeholders match the\nfinal rendered size rather than SizeAwareImage''s default 350px cap.\n\nCentralize layout constants in constants.ts and sass/utils/_variables.scss\nwith cross-reference comments, and wire post_attachment_opengraph.scss to\nthose variables to keep TS layout math and CSS in sync.\n\nAlso hide copy/download utility buttons on link preview images via\nhideUtilities={true}.\n\n* Change the opengraph dimention variables from SCSS to CSS\n\n* Lint and update snapshot\n\n* Add additional E2E test\n\nThis test passes on master in Chrome but not in Firefox.\n\n* Update URL in opengraph-huge.html\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Harrison Healey <harrisonmhealey@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"1efcda3166272f288babb843d8c6b41c2906f116","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/1efcda3166272f288babb843d8c6b41c2906f116"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/81d6d1ea20c07d9394cb569e7dd4da546cfc56fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 1efcda3166272f288babb843d8c6b41c2906f116\nparent 0fc1ff17c8a92a00c2694a059214d0b823db2a83\nauthor Sudheer <sudheer.105@gmail.com> 1786545599 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786545599 -0400\n\nFix link preview image layout shift by using SizeAwareImage (#37357)\n\n* Fix link preview image layout shift by reserving space with SizeAwareImage\n\nOpen graph link previews rendered a plain <img> with no upfront dimensions.\nWhen metadata reported large images (e.g. 2400×1256), the preview started at\nzero height and expanded after load, pushing content below and causing scroll\npop in the channel and permalink views.\n\nUse SizeAwareImage (same approach as post images and message attachments) so\nknown dimensions reserve layout before the image loads. Add\ngetScaledImageDimensions() to scale metadata down to the preview''s CSS limits\n(392×240 for large images, 80×80 for thumbnails) so placeholders match the\nfinal rendered size rather than SizeAwareImage''s default 350px cap.\n\nCentralize layout constants in constants.ts and sass/utils/_variables.scss\nwith cross-reference comments, and wire post_attachment_opengraph.scss to\nthose variables to keep TS layout math and CSS in sync.\n\nAlso hide copy/download utility buttons on link preview images via\nhideUtilities={true}.\n\n* Change the opengraph dimention variables from SCSS to CSS\n\n* Lint and update snapshot\n\n* Add additional E2E test\n\nThis test passes on master in Chrome but not in Firefox.\n\n* Update URL in opengraph-huge.html\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Harrison Healey <harrisonmhealey@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfIW/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN4wQAKsJ2aCsdziJvHQBvU3IuET0\nDTutgQMrvZNJ+cFeCzBx7Rgeb1FM9RdzWCZ+cHmC/KdorLe+JvL4ZkzsABLAua+H\nfmNzkYeGOy9Wv3/k/VDcWxt0ncXSU8x1n5f4Q1ePhFS2zXlz1bnWzTwggFOALobq\ngZVexVDzQvKfPNhVLJ+DyzxPYKjUPZCaMLoWzJgQmwNcrLS6nQcOAwd852/x16Gt\nq0fFhwkuw5FPKcabqWmdQfMS46/3V9USKqe0GfHmqsxHivhcswzcmFKD3Bj2GLh0\nYO+AOW3GqWZO7YI+CaOs+/bT2/9CSDPzX/GQtMQnFce8jM5a0syI+W0Tv8/7VqHn\n5vIPR407HkHlzZqTG7fE0r5Zu8bXIqhSayjDNKREmPIdkGErVDyn0hPuNhVUfDut\naCcrFh7DIasL2T7+pGADzAYCAwTPy6qaiMLqhhROCfquXnSRhiq67WSkgdctpBc3\nloFW0D606iBX7XOat9R7B7n6TAEunhkjASjB1cUkPZggZM7G9q05mM8Y5RAqeqEX\n6HNvxp1HZZYLbJfg+45igDdxO4RBOS/+Nh9yLFqGVdZDZOKG5dIqoEEOXBqu6Wzb\nD3yTyAxnrkkqgRvxDpNRFe8j1OZyf5olPUwaHqPLbN7bEXvlZGIStyrUHWdSWTf5\nVh/OulajgOOvnPDYb3WX\n=Mxnu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T14:40:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/81d6d1ea20c07d9394cb569e7dd4da546cfc56fe","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKDgxZDZkMWVhMjBjMDdkOTM5NGNiNTY5ZTdkZDRkYTU0NmNmYzU2ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/0fc1ff17c8a92a00c2694a059214d0b823db2a83","sha":"0fc1ff17c8a92a00c2694a059214d0b823db2a83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/0fc1ff17c8a92a00c2694a059214d0b823db2a83"}],"sha":"81d6d1ea20c07d9394cb569e7dd4da546cfc56fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/81d6d1ea20c07d9394cb569e7dd4da546cfc56fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/0fc1ff17c8a92a00c2694a059214d0b823db2a83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T12:58:55Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T12:58:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-69557] Fix post actions menu not closing on outside click in mobile view (#37394)\n\n* [MM-69557] Fix post actions menu not closing on outside click in mobile view\n\nIn the narrow/mobile-responsive layout the post actions (\"…\") menu renders\nas a full-height GenericModal. React-bootstrap only dismisses the modal when\nits outer container is clicked directly, but the full-height dialog element\nintercepted every click in the dimmed area around the menu, so clicking\noutside never closed it.\n\nLet clicks on the empty dialog area fall through to the modal container via\npointer-events (scoped to .menuModal) so clicking outside dismisses the menu,\nmatching standard popup behavior, while keeping the menu itself interactive.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69557] Add E2E test for mobile post actions menu outside-click dismissal\n\nAdds a Playwright spec covering the mobile/narrow layout where the post actions\n(\"…\") menu renders as a full-screen modal. Verifies clicking the dimmed area\noutside the menu (both above and below the menu list) dismisses it, and that\nselecting a menu item still works. The outside-click test fails without the\npointer-events fix, so it is coupled to the real behavior.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69557] Use type-only import for PlaywrightExtended in mobile dot menu spec\n\nSatisfies the @typescript-eslint/consistent-type-imports lint rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69557] Don''t treat pointer-events: none as non-focusable in focus trap\n\nThe mobile menu fix sets pointer-events: none on .menuModal (restoring\nauto on .modal-content). useFocusTrap''s isElementVisible() walked the\nancestor chain and rejected any element under a pointer-events: none\nancestor, which broke keyboard focus trapping inside the modal.\n\npointer-events only affects mouse/touch hit-testing, not keyboard\nfocusability, and can be re-enabled on descendants, so remove it from\nthe visibility check. Adds a regression test.\n\n* Address PR feedback: make focus-trap test spy cleanup exception-safe\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"bde730adbe0fd60c423b6c2a08638189a8924a4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/bde730adbe0fd60c423b6c2a08638189a8924a4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/0fc1ff17c8a92a00c2694a059214d0b823db2a83","verification":{"payload":"tree bde730adbe0fd60c423b6c2a08638189a8924a4c\nparent 46102626dbad7473f461307b7be4c98cd387bf4f\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1786539535 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786539535 -0400\n\n[MM-69557] Fix post actions menu not closing on outside click in mobile view (#37394)\n\n* [MM-69557] Fix post actions menu not closing on outside click in mobile view\n\nIn the narrow/mobile-responsive layout the post actions (\"…\") menu renders\nas a full-height GenericModal. React-bootstrap only dismisses the modal when\nits outer container is clicked directly, but the full-height dialog element\nintercepted every click in the dimmed area around the menu, so clicking\noutside never closed it.\n\nLet clicks on the empty dialog area fall through to the modal container via\npointer-events (scoped to .menuModal) so clicking outside dismisses the menu,\nmatching standard popup behavior, while keeping the menu itself interactive.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69557] Add E2E test for mobile post actions menu outside-click dismissal\n\nAdds a Playwright spec covering the mobile/narrow layout where the post actions\n(\"…\") menu renders as a full-screen modal. Verifies clicking the dimmed area\noutside the menu (both above and below the menu list) dismisses it, and that\nselecting a menu item still works. The outside-click test fails without the\npointer-events fix, so it is coupled to the real behavior.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69557] Use type-only import for PlaywrightExtended in mobile dot menu spec\n\nSatisfies the @typescript-eslint/consistent-type-imports lint rule.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69557] Don''t treat pointer-events: none as non-focusable in focus trap\n\nThe mobile menu fix sets pointer-events: none on .menuModal (restoring\nauto on .modal-content). useFocusTrap''s isElementVisible() walked the\nancestor chain and rejected any element under a pointer-events: none\nancestor, which broke keyboard focus trapping inside the modal.\n\npointer-events only affects mouse/touch hit-testing, not keyboard\nfocusability, and can be re-enabled on descendants, so remove it from\nthe visibility check. Adds a regression test.\n\n* Address PR feedback: make focus-trap test spy cleanup exception-safe\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfG4PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3fEQAId9Cy/xY51FKTAZ2UvTjBXA\nPBsKCNDLsrgtLRnDMC5eQLuKUWuvwdSEGvT45maMQt7iaGi4C