PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-12T07:02:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/265f1509fa0ea08464a007995c943b21d0530f9a","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKDI2NWYxNTA5ZmEwZWEwODQ2NGEwMDc5OTVjOTQzYjIxZDA1MzBmOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/1f08ac5bb04372421315c0ebe0e951fbecf3ebb6","sha":"1f08ac5bb04372421315c0ebe0e951fbecf3ebb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/1f08ac5bb04372421315c0ebe0e951fbecf3ebb6"}],"sha":"265f1509fa0ea08464a007995c943b21d0530f9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/265f1509fa0ea08464a007995c943b21d0530f9a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5024605?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/wiggin77","id":5024605,"login":"wiggin77","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMjQ2MDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiggin77","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/1f08ac5bb04372421315c0ebe0e951fbecf3ebb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T20:44:25Z","email":"wiggin77@warpmail.net","name":"Doug Lauder"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T20:44:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"MM-69886: Refresh Channel Members RHS on websocket add and reconnect (#37584)\n\n* MM-69886: Refresh Channel Members RHS on websocket add and reconnect\n\nThe Channel Members RHS (participant list) could omit members in two\ngeneral cases:\n\n- On a user_added websocket event, handleUserAddedEvent recorded the\n  profile-in-channel entry and loaded the profile but never loaded the\n  ChannelMembership. buildProfileList drops any user without a\n  membership, so a member added while the channel was open did not\n  appear until the list was fully reloaded. It also affected members\n  whose profile was already loaded (e.g. after they posted) but who\n  still had no membership. Fetch the membership via getChannelMember\n  when it is missing.\n\n- On websocket reconnect, reconnect() reloads only the current user''s\n  own memberships, never the channel roster, and missed user_added /\n  user_removed events are not replayed on a fresh (non-resumed)\n  connection. Members added or removed while disconnected stayed stale\n  until the channel was re-opened. The RHS now reloads the roster when\n  the websocket connection id changes.\n\nThis extends the reconcile-on-load work from MM-68660 (PR #36964, same\nloadProfilesAndReloadChannelMembers path), which pruned removals only\non channel (re)load and did not cover live adds or reconnects.\n\nFound while re-testing MM-67616 (Shared Channels), where synced members\nwere not reflected in the participant list even though the server-side\nsync was correct.\n\n* Add comment to caution about changing remote cluster service ping frequency.","tree":{"sha":"ac13ac6fa17a60a92c2d1b6ed139f6f033d3b8b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/ac13ac6fa17a60a92c2d1b6ed139f6f033d3b8b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/1f08ac5bb04372421315c0ebe0e951fbecf3ebb6","verification":{"payload":"tree ac13ac6fa17a60a92c2d1b6ed139f6f033d3b8b0\nparent 11cc766dfaa1cbe2c08e8ae7994d8118bfdbffa7\nauthor Doug Lauder <wiggin77@warpmail.net> 1786481065 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786481065 -0400\n\nMM-69886: Refresh Channel Members RHS on websocket add and reconnect (#37584)\n\n* MM-69886: Refresh Channel Members RHS on websocket add and reconnect\n\nThe Channel Members RHS (participant list) could omit members in two\ngeneral cases:\n\n- On a user_added websocket event, handleUserAddedEvent recorded the\n  profile-in-channel entry and loaded the profile but never loaded the\n  ChannelMembership. buildProfileList drops any user without a\n  membership, so a member added while the channel was open did not\n  appear until the list was fully reloaded. It also affected members\n  whose profile was already loaded (e.g. after they posted) but who\n  still had no membership. Fetch the membership via getChannelMember\n  when it is missing.\n\n- On websocket reconnect, reconnect() reloads only the current user''s\n  own memberships, never the channel roster, and missed user_added /\n  user_removed events are not replayed on a fresh (non-resumed)\n  connection. Members added or removed while disconnected stayed stale\n  until the channel was re-opened. The RHS now reloads the roster when\n  the websocket connection id changes.\n\nThis extends the reconcile-on-load work from MM-68660 (PR #36964, same\nloadProfilesAndReloadChannelMembers path), which pruned removals only\non channel (re)load and did not cover live adds or reconnects.\n\nFound while re-testing MM-67616 (Shared Channels), where synced members\nwere not reflected in the participant list even though the server-side\nsync was correct.\n\n* Add comment to caution about changing remote cluster service ping frequency.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqe4mpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj9oQAE0/IBqaDRD4cDaWdaYYqWca\nBSpUQ/Lpg8QKuUOU09TGVA2GNIMjGhPPJevsFgtcS8EZ7x2fk4lur05J4IjgogHz\nM36sToAuuIuAW3a/JfMCyZ2K0/VwCPWrJnNqkz+XjL7BdM+yl+Y9Qrgawg9mu7ki\n0Mztg3DBihzhXl9KVysr8VbgMtOcZd2G/3e8Mne3Kb2o0s9K7qiXpqe5XExjalwl\nGH+AUK7aIVGFbe5DVvQDr1jlcDk8ukR5uNkr1RiV0/ZDRPbiOfuT+Vj6l0cQFOV+\nS2EEPVCrziSJsoF3XJfwqQfQqGGiQBOhk5XYBjmMi++KZnTDKNH//OiiAEzF1SNx\nubo7XjqcIHT1JrKB74qWLQT/043EvuMIBp0MQLTTq0J278MfG/lhlWQzroifEGDm\nr1Px3xb6QSDIyn0YOldIs/JLwEKRYcKlgREURrBFe9h+1Ij5DImvijQ/0yhfIQbv\nlcG2o6bzeYGn+/ID1LX9UW8EesdzqcbfFHPwe57hNNOFWgfI0gvTbBRQhzK7ZZ2w\naGvpbvKsTUDY81Wb61f0Qyvq12MS5LCSv3tA0pePOaoc8VSDS+lgZdL7bWb/R6ca\nSKmcccezzWXGaUyemQxXVXi9+gcDFHiPnqhm1GTBTnaikaoh6EMOzzqz2laOfnMR\nAPz/fcfDAPVhkEom6VsX\n=h05U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T20:44:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/1f08ac5bb04372421315c0ebe0e951fbecf3ebb6","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKDFmMDhhYzViYjA0MzcyNDIxMzE1YzBlYmUwZTk1MWZiZWNmM2ViYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/11cc766dfaa1cbe2c08e8ae7994d8118bfdbffa7","sha":"11cc766dfaa1cbe2c08e8ae7994d8118bfdbffa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/11cc766dfaa1cbe2c08e8ae7994d8118bfdbffa7"}],"sha":"1f08ac5bb04372421315c0ebe0e951fbecf3ebb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/1f08ac5bb04372421315c0ebe0e951fbecf3ebb6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/11cc766dfaa1cbe2c08e8ae7994d8118bfdbffa7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:29:01Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T19:29:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[MM-69726] Fix Message actions menu displaying off screen in narrow display (#37396)\n\n* [MM-69726] Fix Message actions menu rendering off screen in narrow view\n\nIn mobile/single-column view the post Message actions menu renders as a\nfull-screen fixed overlay. Because posts live inside the virtualized post\nlist, whose `will-change: transform` establishes a containing block for\nfixed-position descendants, the overlay anchored to the scrolled post list\ncontent instead of the viewport. For longer channels/threads this pushed the\nmenu off screen (to the top of the message pane) so it appeared to do nothing.\n\nPortal the mobile Message actions menu to document.body so its fixed overlay\nis positioned relative to the viewport, and extend the mobile overlay styles\nto the portaled container.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Keep portaled Message actions menu open until item click resolves\n\nThe mobile Message actions menu is portaled to the body, so it lives outside\nthe MenuWrapper node in the DOM. MenuWrapper''s capture-phase blur handler\ntreated clicks inside the portaled menu as outside clicks and closed the menu\nbefore the item''s onClick fired (synchronously under the legacy React root),\nso selecting an item did nothing. Mark the portal and skip blur-close for\nclicks inside it.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Add tests for portaled mobile Message actions menu\n\nCover that the ActionsMenu portals its menu to the body in mobile view and\nrenders inline on desktop, and that MenuWrapper''s blur handling keeps a\nportaled menu open while still closing on genuine outside clicks.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Add integration coverage for portaled menu item clicks\n\nAdd a test that clicking an item in the portaled mobile Message actions menu\nruns its action (the exact behavior the blur-handler fix restored), and a TAB\nkeyboard test mirroring the click-based portal exception.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Clarify portaled menu item test name\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Fix import order in actions_menu test\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Move portaled-menu blur handling out of generic MenuWrapper\n\nReplace the hardcoded [data-menu-portal] selector in MenuWrapper.closeOnBlur\nwith a generic, opt-in portalNodeRef prop. ActionsMenu now owns the portal\ndetail and passes its portal node ref, keeping the generic (deprecated) widget\nfree of consumer-specific conditions.\n\n* [MM-69726] Satisfy jsx-max-props-per-line in menu wrapper test\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","tree":{"sha":"3ee0774a804c7fbbeae18e6eb502b878e2556b76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/3ee0774a804c7fbbeae18e6eb502b878e2556b76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/11cc766dfaa1cbe2c08e8ae7994d8118bfdbffa7","verification":{"payload":"tree 3ee0774a804c7fbbeae18e6eb502b878e2556b76\nparent d3c26275b651b2e23b173c9c914b5fc99e7626b8\nauthor cursor[bot] <206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1786476541 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786476541 -0400\n\n[MM-69726] Fix Message actions menu displaying off screen in narrow display (#37396)\n\n* [MM-69726] Fix Message actions menu rendering off screen in narrow view\n\nIn mobile/single-column view the post Message actions menu renders as a\nfull-screen fixed overlay. Because posts live inside the virtualized post\nlist, whose `will-change: transform` establishes a containing block for\nfixed-position descendants, the overlay anchored to the scrolled post list\ncontent instead of the viewport. For longer channels/threads this pushed the\nmenu off screen (to the top of the message pane) so it appeared to do nothing.\n\nPortal the mobile Message actions menu to document.body so its fixed overlay\nis positioned relative to the viewport, and extend the mobile overlay styles\nto the portaled container.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Keep portaled Message actions menu open until item click resolves\n\nThe mobile Message actions menu is portaled to the body, so it lives outside\nthe MenuWrapper node in the DOM. MenuWrapper''s capture-phase blur handler\ntreated clicks inside the portaled menu as outside clicks and closed the menu\nbefore the item''s onClick fired (synchronously under the legacy React root),\nso selecting an item did nothing. Mark the portal and skip blur-close for\nclicks inside it.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Add tests for portaled mobile Message actions menu\n\nCover that the ActionsMenu portals its menu to the body in mobile view and\nrenders inline on desktop, and that MenuWrapper''s blur handling keeps a\nportaled menu open while still closing on genuine outside clicks.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Add integration coverage for portaled menu item clicks\n\nAdd a test that clicking an item in the portaled mobile Message actions menu\nruns its action (the exact behavior the blur-handler fix restored), and a TAB\nkeyboard test mirroring the click-based portal exception.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Clarify portaled menu item test name\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Fix import order in actions_menu test\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-69726] Move portaled-menu blur handling out of generic MenuWrapper\n\nReplace the hardcoded [data-menu-portal] selector in MenuWrapper.closeOnBlur\nwith a generic, opt-in portalNodeRef prop. ActionsMenu now owns the portal\ndetail and passes its portal node ref, keeping the generic (deprecated) widget\nfree of consumer-specific conditions.\n\n* [MM-69726] Satisfy jsx-max-props-per-line in menu wrapper test\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqe3f9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu+oQAKVk7KHnctuRHRTW/IRwdoKT\nrF3D/JzQGqF/icPtDfRiG24gH0RY9B95fAW1uCFZQy01RpY9EQNYlu2WSO7MM66W\n+gUxcSsvJBLxAoOhKFaGpoGl/2BBeW2dPce4Mj8xEHeQ+Wazh/77eUHg6DY2Q2cR\noOAAwDiWbdE/Dl1ss9G8dNvxW2vdlcmoK6UaSpXsSMXSfDN8PtTFEX+nkUyQa2JD\nDimLedwxbzgneOIXYS+xPb/DrN8hjk0qLV+bEyI6FSP5/EDm7n9tRo1Orw9nnT/k\n9Mql4iXdZHwlcG3/nlGvCIezVkpB8Nrp7+YiKi8a8AfPTVliofaU+sX1mfJzwAPn\nGNGFli6LeaEPkKGkODE0hoKF+vwpIRRfLpBcJdB+6QhVTTxbfjqbwHSnekluw+xT\nMou3hbGSBo8y+i2qN/GQ33wR1kTa/6iIo2Rmv6gMdDDQ1fY0FMKNs1m+NOqThsbO\noWS3OEPCZC3JEwR+ru1mWdxTqMh4RWipDljBRhUfWvyC63Lhv2Im6m1ZYxdoFvnu\nl5I0udbG8eigW59Q6UkuYGfwprv3RfgBqWPbPhtdCTAySp7g5cQ0cxt89K2OCukt\nLdu7MZdDgHlSSN5ourlHyVf21VuSbqk0Ld5UnQcDqZyxDx7d4oxWrQd5WkDP8DA6\nteDkCMHzL0qvn560sUJn\n=X1vf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T19:29:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/11cc766dfaa1cbe2c08e8ae7994d8118bfdbffa7","node_id":"C_kwDORDiVY9oAKDExY2M3NjZkZmFhMWNiZTJjMDhlOGFlNzk5NGQ4MTE4YmZkYmZmYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commit/d3c26275b651b2e23b173c9c914b5fc99e7626b8","sha":"d3c26275b651b2e23b173c9c914b5fc99e7626b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/d3c26275b651b2e23b173c9c914b5fc99e7626b8"}],"sha":"11cc766dfaa1cbe2c08e8ae7994d8118bfdbffa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/11cc766dfaa1cbe2c08e8ae7994d8118bfdbffa7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/785518?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/JulienTant","id":785518,"login":"JulienTant","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4NTUxOA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JulienTant","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/commits/d3c26275b651b2e23b173c9c914b5fc99e7626b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:28:58Z","email":"785518+JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Julien Tant"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:28:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mmctl): lengthen sampledata passwords to meet FIPS minimum (#37867)\n\n* fix(mmctl): lengthen sampledata passwords to meet FIPS minimum\n\nZero-pad user index to 3 digits in guest and regular-user password\nformat strings so all generated passwords are >= 14 characters,\nmatching PasswordFIPSMinimumLength. Update inject-test-data login\nhint and add a regression test.\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Simplify sampledata password length test comment\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Use subtests in sampledata password length coverage\n\nSo a single require failure reports only that case instead of\naborting the rest of the matrix.\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Name default-user subtests as user for clarity\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Run sampledata password length subtests in parallel\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Empty commit to re-trigger CI\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"79b77f831a66dbf7a9258d4a391aec055e31865d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/trees/79b77f831a66dbf7a9258d4a391aec055e31865d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Unity-Billal-mesloub/mattermost/git/commits/d3c26275b651b2e23b173c9c914b5fc99e7626b8","verification":{"payload":"tree 79b77f831a66dbf7a9258d4a391aec055e31865d\nparent 844d3370b71f49ede1ef3a4bfbc22c80a8bd135f\nauthor Julien Tant <785518+JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com> 1786469338 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786469338 +0000\n\nfix(mmctl): lengthen sampledata passwords to meet FIPS minimum (#37867)\n\n* fix(mmctl): lengthen sampledata passwords to meet FIPS minimum\n\nZero-pad user index to 3 digits in guest and regular-user password\nformat strings so all generated passwords are >= 14 characters,\nmatching PasswordFIPSMinimumLength. Update inject-test-data login\nhint and add a regression test.\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Simplify sampledata password length test comment\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Use subtests in sampledata password length coverage\n\nSo a single require failure reports only that case instead of\naborting the rest of the matrix.\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Name default-user subtests as user for clarity\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Run sampledata password length subtests in parallel\n\nCo-authored-by: Julien Tant <JulienTant@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Empty commit to re-trigger CI\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Julien Ta